  "scout_brief": "Integrate crawl4ai (https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai) into arXMCP to add a paper-discovery capability: given a notebook's topic area (e.g. 'Bridgeland stability conditions'), autonomously go discover NEW arXiv papers in that area and add them as additional context to the notebook. The stated goal/hope from the user is that crawl4ai-based scraping could sidestep arXiv's rate-limiting. Scope: (1) whether crawl4ai is the right tool vs arXiv official API/OAI-PMH which arXMCP already uses, (2) the rate-limiting / arXiv ToS reality, (3) how a discover-related-papers-for-a-notebook feature would fit arXMCP existing ingest pipeline + MCP tool surface + notebook model, (4) the local-first / no-fork / no-Node constraints. Heavy bias toward concrete deltas vs arXMCP current ingest capability.",
